{{also|Donga|dóŋa}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|en|af|donga}}, from {{der|en|zu|udonga}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdɔŋɡə/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdɒŋɡə/}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|South Africa}} A usually dry, eroded watercourse running only in times of heavy rain.
#: {{synonyms|en|arroyo|wadi|wash}}
#* '''1900''', [[w:Arthur Conan Doyle|Arthur Conan Doyle]], ''[[w:The Great Boer War|The Great Boer War]]'', Volume 2, 2008 Easyread Large Bold Edition, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=n9OgrzHWUg8C&pg=PA14&dq=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=409CT7zxOMiRiQfo66G5BA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 14]:
#*: Major Pack-Beresford and other officers were shot down, and every unhorsed man remained necessarily as a prisoner under the very muzzles of the riflemen in the '''donga'''.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1901|author=[[w:Ernest William Hornung|Ernest William Hornung]]|chapter=The Knees of the Gods|title=[[w:The Black Mask|Raffles: Further Adventures of the Amateur Cracksman]]|publisher=Charles Scribner’s Sons|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=g8oWAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA284&dq=donga|page=284
|passage=There were trenches for us men, but no place of safety for our horses nearer than this long and narrow '''donga''' which ran from within our lines towards those of the Boers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1948|author=[[w:Henry Vollam Morton|Henry Vollam Morton]]|title=In Search of South Africa|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=CTRCAAAAIAAJ|publisher=Methuen|page=168
|passage=Thousands of miserable cattle and goats roamed everywhere making tracks that would someday form cracks which successive rains would open into gullies and '''dongas'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1999|author={{w|JM Coetzee}}|title=Disgrace|page=98|publisher=Vintage|year_published=2000
|passage=Count yourself lucky not to be a prisoner in the car at this moment, speeding away, or at the bottom of a '''donga''' with a bullet in your head.}}

